      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(oc-path): bound config file reads with size cap",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTwo unbounded file reads in `extensions/oc-path/src/cli.ts`:\n\n1. `loadAst` (line 164): reads the entire config file into memory to parse as JSONC/JSONL/YAML/Markdown AST, with no size limit\n2. `set` command diff read (line 335): reads the \"old\" file content for `--diff` output, with no size limit\n\nBoth paths use user-supplied CLI arguments (`openclaw path resolve <file>`, `openclaw path set <file>`) — a user could accidentally point to a large file and OOM the CLI.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUnbounded `fs.readFile` on user-controlled paths is a valid OOM vector. While oc-path files are typically small config files, there is no defense against multi-GB input.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdded `loadOcPathFileSafely` helper that:\n1. Stats the file via `statSync`\n2. Rejects non-regular files\n3. Rejects files exceeding 10 MiB\n4. Only reads files that pass the checks\n\nApplied to both the `loadAst` path and the `set --diff` path.\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `openclaw path resolve ./10GB-config.json` → OOM | → rejected with \"file too large\" |\n| `openclaw path set ./10GB-config.json key value` → OOM | → rejected with \"file too large\" |\n| Normal small config files → works | → works (unchanged) |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 698 oc-path tests pass:**\n\n```\n✓ extensions/oc-path (40 test files, 698 passed)\n```",
        "branch": "fix/bound-oc-path-cli",
